{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Leo, I'm sorry this has been frustrating, and I understand you've had to ask more than once. I checked your laptop and the cause is clear: the drive is almost full, with only about 9 GB (3.5%) free out of 256 GB. That's why it can't save files. Please try these steps now: 1) Empty your Recycle Bin and clear out your Downloads folder. 2) Open Settings, then System, then Storage, and select Temporary files. Remove the temporary files and any old Windows Update files. 3) If you use OneDrive, turn on Files On-Demand so synced files stay in the cloud until you open them. 4) Uninstall any apps you no longer use. Once you've done this, please reply to this ticket and we'll re-check the free space. If it's still very low after cleanup, we'll look at a larger drive or a replacement laptop.",
  "internal_note": "Sender Leo Martins (user_id 6, Sales, America/New_York, usual hours 09:00-17:00, account active, no lockout, not blocked, password set 2026-09-11). Device BL-LT-0106 (Windows 11 Pro) is online, last check-in 2026-10-11 03:01 UTC. Disk: 256 GB total, 9 GB free, 3.5% free, warning 'Low disk space'. This matches KB-017 (under 10% free causes file save failures). No user-side cleanup has been done yet, and the technician cannot run it remotely from our tools. Next step: user performs KB-017 cleanup, then re-run check_device_status. Escalate to Tier 2 (larger drive or replacement) if free space stays under 10% after cleanup. Ticket is repeat contact (second request), so prioritize a quick response on the follow-up. No account actions taken.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-017"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
